WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.514
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel. Welcome to Online Intermediate.

2
00:00:04.814 --> 00:00:08.143
Hi! I'm Nita. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.443 --> 00:00:14.183
Unit two: Work-Life Balance. In this unit, you will talk about work, stress and free time.

4
00:00:15.183 --> 00:00:16.057
workload.

5
00:00:16.757 --> 00:00:19.476
workload means the amount of work a person has to do.

6
00:00:19.776 --> 00:00:22.368
My workload has doubled since my colleague left.

7
00:00:23.068 --> 00:00:25.302
Your turn. Say: workload.

8
00:00:28.002 --> 00:00:28.887
workload.

9
00:00:29.883 --> 00:00:30.687
burnout.

10
00:00:31.387 --> 00:00:35.418
burnout means extreme tiredness caused by working too hard for too long.

11
00:00:35.718 --> 00:00:38.229
She took a month off to recover from burnout.

12
00:00:38.929 --> 00:00:40.873
Your turn. Say: burnout.

13
00:00:43.573 --> 00:00:44.388
burnout.

14
00:00:45.383 --> 00:00:46.721
flexible hours.

15
00:00:47.421 --> 00:00:51.812
flexible hours means a system where you can choose when you start and finish work.

16
00:00:52.112 --> 00:00:55.192
Flexible hours let parents pick up their children from school.

17
00:00:55.892 --> 00:00:58.973
Your turn. Say: flexible hours.

18
00:01:01.673 --> 00:01:03.081
flexible hours.

19
00:01:04.083 --> 00:01:05.108
commute time.

20
00:01:05.808 --> 00:01:09.049
commute time means the time it takes to travel to and from work.

21
00:01:09.349 --> 00:01:11.616
His commute time is over an hour each way.

22
00:01:12.316 --> 00:01:15.003
Your turn. Say: commute time.

23
00:01:17.703 --> 00:01:18.728
commute time.

24
00:01:19.717 --> 00:01:20.904
deadline pressure.

25
00:01:21.604 --> 00:01:26.041
deadline pressure means stress caused by having to finish work by a certain time.

26
00:01:26.341 --> 00:01:28.770
Deadline pressure makes some people work better.

27
00:01:29.470 --> 00:01:32.099
Your turn. Say: deadline pressure.

28
00:01:34.799 --> 00:01:36.160
deadline pressure.

29
00:01:37.150 --> 00:01:38.186
work from home.

30
00:01:38.886 --> 00:01:42.302
work from home means to do your job at home instead of in an office.

31
00:01:42.602 --> 00:01:44.880
I work from home on Mondays and Fridays.

32
00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:47.814
Your turn. Say: work from home.

33
00:01:50.514 --> 00:01:51.562
work from home.

34
00:01:52.550 --> 00:01:53.760
overtime pay.

35
00:01:54.460 --> 00:01:58.155
overtime pay means extra money for working more than your normal hours.

36
00:01:58.455 --> 00:02:00.849
Factory workers get overtime pay at weekends.

37
00:02:01.549 --> 00:02:04.201
Your turn. Say: overtime pay.

38
00:02:06.901 --> 00:02:08.077
overtime pay.

39
00:02:09.083 --> 00:02:10.038
annual leave.

40
00:02:10.738 --> 00:02:13.910
annual leave means paid holiday days you get from your job each year.

41
00:02:14.210 --> 00:02:16.616
I've already used half of my annual leave this year.

42
00:02:17.316 --> 00:02:19.411
Your turn. Say: annual leave.

43
00:02:22.111 --> 00:02:23.321
annual leave.

44
00:02:24.317 --> 00:02:26.444
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:26.744 --> 00:02:29.373
You look tired, Nita. Have you been sleeping well?

46
00:02:30.683 --> 00:02:33.870
Not really. My workload has been huge this month.

47
00:02:35.183 --> 00:02:37.160
Have you talked to your manager about it?

48
00:02:38.450 --> 00:02:42.194
Yes, I did last week. She offered me flexible hours.

49
00:02:43.483 --> 00:02:46.089
That's great. Burnout is a serious problem.

50
00:02:47.383 --> 00:02:50.767
I know. I've also booked some annual leave for April.

51
00:02:52.083 --> 00:02:55.464
Grammar focus: Present perfect vs past simple.

52
00:02:55.764 --> 00:02:59.761
Use the present perfect for experiences and for time that is not finished.

53
00:03:00.061 --> 00:03:02.978
Use the past simple for a finished time in the past.

54
00:03:03.278 --> 00:03:07.950
For example: I have worked here for two years. I worked late last night.

55
00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:13.210
Use the past simple with finished time words like yesterday, last week and in 2020.

56
00:03:14.217 --> 00:03:16.660
Now read and listen. The Four-Day Week.

57
00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:20.295
Several companies around the world have tried a four-day working week.

58
00:03:21.583 --> 00:03:24.755
Workers kept the same salary but worked one day less.

59
00:03:26.050 --> 00:03:29.060
Many employees said that their workload felt more manageable.

60
00:03:30.350 --> 00:03:33.673
Managers reported less burnout and fewer sick days.

61
00:03:34.983 --> 00:03:38.840
However, some businesses found it difficult to serve customers every day.

62
00:03:40.150 --> 00:03:42.489
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

63
00:03:42.789 --> 00:03:45.671
Extreme tiredness from working too much is called blank.

64
00:03:45.971 --> 00:03:49.555
A, overtime pay. B, burnout. C, annual leave.

65
00:03:53.550 --> 00:03:55.944
The answer is B: burnout.

66
00:03:57.450 --> 00:04:00.309
I blank in this company since 2022.

67
00:04:00.609 --> 00:04:03.159
A, worked. B, have worked. C, work.

68
00:04:07.150 --> 00:04:08.999
The answer is B: have worked.

69
00:04:10.483 --> 00:04:11.868
She blank late yesterday.

70
00:04:12.168 --> 00:04:15.658
A, has stayed. B, stayed. C, stays.

71
00:04:19.650 --> 00:04:21.081
The answer is B: stayed.

72
00:04:22.583 --> 00:04:25.047
Paid holiday days from your job are called blank.

73
00:04:25.347 --> 00:04:28.722
A, annual leave. B, commute time. C, workload.

74
00:04:32.717 --> 00:04:34.623
The answer is A: annual leave.

75
00:04:36.117 --> 00:04:39.579
According to the text, workers in the four-day week blank.

76
00:04:39.879 --> 00:04:44.601
A, earned less. B, kept the same salary. C, worked longer days.

77
00:04:48.617 --> 00:04:51.173
The answer is B: kept the same salary.

78
00:04:52.683 --> 00:04:56.624
Now it's your turn to speak. How do you balance work or study with free time?

79
00:05:01.924 --> 00:05:06.966
I try to finish my work by six o'clock, and I always keep Sunday for my family.

80
00:05:07.266 --> 00:05:08.847
Excellent answer, Nita!

81
00:05:09.850 --> 00:05:14.372
Great work today! You learned eight new words and present perfect vs past simple.

82
00:05:14.672 --> 00:05:18.032
Today's value is good habits. Do good things every day.

83
00:05:18.332 --> 00:05:20.543
See you in Unit three. Goodbye!

84
00:05:20.843 --> 00:05:23.681
Thank you, Mr. Daniel! Bye, everyone!

